cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BioExplainR, cite this software snapshot. Version DOI will be added only after archival publication."
type: software
title: "BioExplainR: fact-constrained explanations and traceable checks for bioinformatics R results"
authors:
  - name: "BioExplainR contributors"
version: "0.4.0.9000"
date-released: "2026-10-08"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  BioExplainR computes deterministic facts from existing R bioinformatics results,
  optionally uses language models to organise explanations, checks explicit claims
  and supported plot mappings, and reports project dependencies and sample coverage.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - R
  - reproducibility
  - explanation
